Proxy Metaprogramming
The two objects
Proxy
and
Reflect
allow for programming at the meta level in JavaScript.
Proxy
can be used to
intercept property operations
like reading or writing.
In the example below:
A user object is
wrapped in a Proxy
The Proxy uses a
set() trap
to log whenever a property is set
